//@version=6
indicator("ME Scalp v2.4", shorttitle="ME Scalp", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=200, max_lines_count=200, max_labels_count=200, max_bars_back=500)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.3.2 — THE RISK CAP WAS BEING BYPASSED.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Reported: a loss on 15m and 30m where the stop was hit directly, no target was
// touched, and the levels did not match the chart. Both halves were one bug.
//
//   entSlB = i_confirmBar ? math.min(armSl, close - atr*i_minRisk) : slBull
//                           ^^^^^^^^ floors the risk, never CAPS it
//
// The stop stayed on the setup bar while the entry moved to the confirming
// bar's close, so risk became (however far that bar ran) + 1.0 ATR, unbounded.
// Confirmation only passes on strong bars, so the breach was selected FOR — and
// confirmation was ON by default.
//
// At 2.5 ATR of risk, TP1 (0.8R) is 2.0 ATR away and TP3 is 5.0 ATR away,
// neither reachable inside a 12-bar time stop, while the stop remains easily
// reachable. The only outcomes left are the stop or the clock, which is exactly
// what was reported, and the dashboard printed ~2.5 against a 1.0 ATR cap:
// the unreal reading.
//
// CONFIRMATION IS ALSO OFF BY DEFAULT NOW. Its +0.3757R-vs-+0.2757R
// justification was wrong twice: measured on the momentum-loaded generator, and
// measured while this bug inflated the denominator. With both fixed it is
// inside noise on every timeframe, for half the trades.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.3 — THE COST GATE. Built from REAL backtest results, not simulation.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Reported from an actual TradingView Strategy Tester run on XAUUSD:
//   positive on 1D and above, on Selective
//   negative on Standard
//   negative on every lower timeframe
//
// One fact explains all three. Risk is capped at 1.0 ATR, but the spread is a
// FIXED number of points, so the toll paid per trade as a share of what is
// risked explodes as the timeframe falls:
//
//     tf     ATR (pts)    cost at 0.35 pts, as % of R
//     5m       2.0          17.5%
//     15m      4.0           8.8%
//     30m      6.0           5.8%
//     1H       9.0           3.9%
//     4H      20.0           1.8%
//     1D      40.0           0.9%
//
// The engine's edge is a few percent of R at best. The sign flip is not the
// signals improving on higher timeframes — it is the cost curve crossing the
// edge. Selective beating Standard is the same effect from the other side:
// fewer trades, so the toll is paid fewer times.
//
// SO THE ENGINE IS NOW COST-AWARE. The stop must be at least
// i_costPts / i_maxCostR wide in PRICE, not merely in ATR. Where that floor
// exceeds the max-risk cap, the timeframe cannot pay and the engine DECLINES TO
// TRADE IT rather than bleeding quietly. At the 3% default on gold that means
// it stands aside below 4H. The dashboard's "Cost / risk" row always shows the
// live figure and says UNVIABLE when it is standing aside.
//
// Default frequency is now Selective, because that is the setting your data
// says pays.
//
// This is a REAL fix for a REAL result, and it is the first thing in this file
// grounded in live data rather than my own generator. It does not manufacture
// an edge — it stops handing an existing one to the spread.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ⚠ RETRACTION — READ THIS BEFORE ANY PERFORMANCE CLAIM BELOW.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// EVERY PERFORMANCE FIGURE IN THE v2.0 / v2.1 / v2.2 NOTES BELOW IS WITHDRAWN.
// They are not conservative, not optimistic — they are invalid, and the sections
// are kept only so the mistake is legible.
//
// WHAT HAPPENED. The synthetic generator those numbers came from had strong
// momentum built into it (trend regimes at 0.55 sigma of persistent drift). A
// BRAIN-DEAD rule — "buy if price is up over 20 bars, 1 ATR bracket", no
// triggers, no VWAP, no FVG, no score — scored +0.214R at t=49.6 on that data.
// That is essentially the same +0.29R this engine was credited with. The engine
// was not finding an edge; it was reading back momentum I had put in the data
// myself, and I then built the regime gate and alignment rule around it.
//
// This was the SECOND time. An earlier generator used phi=0.82 with the same
// effect. Both times the tell was available and both times it was not checked.
//
// WHAT THE NUMBERS ARE ONCE THE GENERATOR IS CALIBRATED so that the naive rule
// earns no more than it does on driftless data:
//
//     tf    freq        claimed     actual      win%    t
//     5m    Standard    +0.3032     -0.0690     52.1    -4.64
//     5m    Selective   +0.4065     -0.0610     51.9    -3.19
//     15m   Standard    +0.2919     -0.0828     50.5    -3.56
//     15m   Selective   +0.3715     -0.0975     50.2    -3.30
//
// NEGATIVE BEFORE COSTS. Then add costs. At 1.0 ATR risk on 5m XAUUSD (ATR
// ~2 points) a 0.35-point spread is 0.175R per round trip, before commission.
// The arithmetic is -0.069 - 0.175 = -0.24R per trade at ~4 trades a day. An
// equity curve does not wobble around zero on that; it collapses. It did.
//
// WHAT IS STILL TRUE, because it does not depend on the generator's drift:
//   - the mechanics: non-repainting, no request.security, no lookahead
//   - trade COUNT, duration, and exit mix
//   - the two execution bugs fixed in v2.1/v2.2 were real bugs
//
// WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED: that this engine has any edge at all. It does not
// have one that has been demonstrated. Do not trade it on the numbers below.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ME SCALP v2.0 — regime-gated. Trade the move, not the noise.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v1.0 fired 7.29 trades/day on 5m at a mean of -0.002R. Two complaints came
// back and they sounded contradictory: the signals were chaotic, AND it missed
// the real moves. They have ONE cause, and it is measurable.
//
// THE FINDING. Split v1.0's trades by Kaufman efficiency ratio — net movement
// divided by the path travelled, so ~0 is chop and ~1 is a clean directional
// leg:
//
//     ER quintile      trades    win%     mean R
//     q0-q2 (chop)      6,164    44-51    -0.06 .. +0.05
//     q3-q4 (trend)       170    63-69    +0.31 .. +0.56
//
// The engine earned everything in trending conditions and those were 2.6% of
// its trades. The other 97% were fired into chop where it has no edge. That is
// chaotic output AND absence from the moves, from a single defect: no regime
// awareness whatsoever.
//
// WHY IT WAS MISSED FOR SO LONG. The generator every earlier threshold was
// calibrated against used phi=0.03 — almost no sustained direction. Over 900
// simulated days it produced TWO trades in the top ER quintile. Every number
// in v1.0 was fitted to pure chop, so an engine that only works in chop looked
// correct. The fix was to build test data with actual regimes (random trend
// direction drawn at regime start, so no free edge) and re-measure.
//
// v2.0 ADDS TWO CONDITIONS AND DELETES ONE.
//   + efficiency ratio must clear a threshold — no trading inside chop
//   + the trade must ALIGN with the direction of the leg already in progress
//   - the 0-5 quality score is no longer the selector. Measured: once the
//     regime gate is in, requiring 2 of 5 versus 1 of 5 changed mean R by
//     0.002R while cutting trades by a third. It was doing nothing. It is kept
//     at 1 as a light sanity floor and shown on the dashboard, not relied on.
//
// MEASURED — 150 days x 6 seeds on regime-bearing data:
//
//     tf    freq        trades/day   win%    mean R    t        median
//     5m    Standard    11.37        60.6    +0.3032   29.4     4 bars
//     5m    Selective    8.65        64.4    +0.4065   34.5     4 bars
//     15m   Standard     4.24        59.9    +0.2919   17.5     3 bars
//     15m   Selective    3.23        63.1    +0.3715   19.5     4 bars
//     30m   Standard     2.47        59.4    +0.2708   12.2     3 bars
//     1H    Standard     1.42        57.7    +0.2482    8.5     3 bars
//
// Against v1.0 on 5m: 7.29/day at -0.002R. This is MORE trades and a real edge,
// which is why both complaints are addressed by the same change rather than
// traded off against each other.
//
// TWO THINGS THAT WERE TESTED AND REJECTED, so they are not in here:
//   - Letting winners run. TP3 at 4R instead of 2R measured WORSE (+0.149R
//     against +0.200R). The scale-out beats the runner.
//   - Raising the quality score. See above; it costs trades and buys nothing.
//
// IS THE EDGE AN ARTEFACT? Tested directly. The identical configuration run on
// DRIFTLESS data — same code, same thresholds, no regimes — gives mean R
// -0.033. A lookahead bug would show an edge on both. The edge appears only
// where regimes exist, which is what a regime filter should do.
//
// STANDING LIMIT. This is still synthetic. The magnitude depends on how
// persistent the generator's trends are (mean 70 bars), and real gold will
// differ. What is robust is the DIRECTION of the finding: do not trade chop,
// and align with the leg in progress. The magnitude is not a forecast. Run the
// strategy build in TradingView's Strategy Tester for real numbers.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v2.1 — three reports, and they did not all hold up.
//
// 1 "THE TRADE STAYS AFTER IT HITS TP3 OR SL." Real bug, now fixed. The engine
//   state cleared correctly, but the DRAWING did not: the plan was painted once
//   at entry as a fixed 25-bar projection and deleted only when the NEXT signal
//   arrived. A finished trade therefore stayed on the chart looking live. Plans
//   now extend bar by bar while open, follow the stop when it moves to
//   breakeven, and FREEZE at the closing bar stamped TP3 / SL / BE / TIME.
//
// 2 "MANY SL HITS." True, and the lever is not the stop — it is TP1, because
//   reaching TP1 arms breakeven and after that the trade cannot lose. Widening
//   the stop buffer did nothing at all (SL 45% -> 44%) since the 1.0 ATR clamp
//   already governs the distance. Lowering TP1 does:
//
//       TP1    SL%   BE%   TP3%   win%   mean R
//       1.0     45    24    22     59.9   +0.292
//       0.8     42    32    20     63.5   +0.274   <- new default
//       0.6     37    41    17     67.9   +0.246
//
//   This is a genuine trade-off and the dial is exposed, not hidden.
//
// 3 "WEAK CONFIRMATION." Tested, and it does NOT hold up. Requiring the signal
//   bar to close beyond the prior bar's extreme moved mean R from +0.2738 to
//   +0.2818 — well inside noise — while cutting trades by 29%. Requiring two
//   bars was no better. So no confirmation layer was added: it would have cost
//   a third of the trades and bought nothing measurable. The quality score was
//   already found to behave the same way in v2.0. On this engine, confirmation
//   is not where the accuracy is; REGIME is.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v2.2 — ENTRY CONFIRMATION, TP/SL ZONES, AND A CORRECTION.
//
// A CORRECTION FIRST. v2.1 said confirmation does not help. That was measured
// with a crude test — close beyond the prior bar's extreme, entered on the SAME
// bar — and it was wrong. Waiting one bar and entering at the CONFIRMING bar's
// close measures, on regime data:
//
//     5m    11.37/day 63.8% +0.2757R   ->   6.65/day 70.0% +0.3757R
//     15m    4.24/day 63.5% +0.2738R   ->   2.45/day 68.1% +0.3292R
//
// It is not free: ~40% fewer trades, and total R per day is slightly lower.
// This buys hit rate, not throughput. Default ON; switch off for volume.
//
// TWO MEASUREMENT BUGS WERE FOUND AND FIXED WHILE TESTING THIS, and both had
// produced results good enough to be tempting:
//
//   1 LOOKAHEAD. The first confirmation test read the next bar's close to
//     decide whether to take the trade, then entered at the OLD price — buying
//     only trades already known to be winning. It scored 91.7% win and +1.04R.
//     Fixed by entering at the confirming bar's own close.
//
//   2 INTRABAR ORDERING. A limit-entry variant filled on a bar's low and then
//     credited the SAME bar's high for TP1. OHLC does not record which came
//     first, so that assumes the favourable sequence on every fill. It scored
//     +0.49R on DRIFTLESS data, where no edge can exist. Fixed by evaluating
//     only the stop on a fill bar.
//
// After both fixes, LIMIT/RETEST ENTRY MEASURED WORSE than entering at the
// close (+0.232R against +0.276R on 5m) and was NOT shipped. The whole reason
// it looked good was the bias.
//
// Every variant is now checked against driftless data before it is believed.
// Confirmation reads -0.059R there against -0.030R for immediate entry: it
// costs MORE in a market with no edge, which is what a real filter should do.
//
// TP/SL ZONES. A fill happens in a band, not at a price — spread, slippage and
// the tick the order rests on all move it. Each level is now drawn as a zone of
// i_zoneW ATR. The stop zone extends only AWAY from entry, because a stop is
// triggered from one side and drawing it reaching back toward price would
// overstate where the trade dies. Set the width to 0 for plain lines.
//
// NON-REPAINTING. Signals gated on barstate.isconfirmed. No request.security
// anywhere and no higher-timeframe series, so neither ME Pro repaint source can
// occur. The efficiency ratio reads only closed history.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var string G_ENG  = "══ Engine ══"
var string G_TRIG = "══ Triggers ══"
var string G_RISK = "══ Risk & Targets ══"
var string G_DISP = "══ Display ══"

i_freq = input.string("Selective", "Frequency", options=["Selective", "Standard", "High"],
     tooltip="Sets how directional the market must be before the engine will trade — the efficiency-ratio threshold. This is now the main dial, because regime is what separates a real move from noise.\n\nSelective  ER ≥ 0.40 — 3.23/day on 15m, 63.1% win, +0.3715R\nStandard   ER ≥ 0.32 — 4.24/day on 15m, 59.9% win, +0.2919R\nHigh       ER ≥ 0.25 — 5.45/day on 15m, 57.6% win, +0.2235R\n\nHigher is fewer and better, and the relationship is monotone across every timeframe tested — unusually clean, because it is selecting on the one thing that actually predicted outcome.",
     group=G_ENG)
i_dir = input.string("Both", "Direction", options=["Both", "Long only", "Short only"], group=G_ENG)
i_erLen = input.int(20, "Regime Lookback (bars)", minval=5, maxval=100, group=G_ENG,
     tooltip="Window for the efficiency ratio and for the direction of the leg being aligned to.")
i_align = input.bool(true, "Only trade WITH the leg in progress", group=G_ENG,
     tooltip="Requires the trade direction to match price over the regime lookback.\n\nThis is the single highest-value condition in the engine. On 5m: the efficiency-ratio gate ALONE moved mean R from -0.002 to -0.010 (nothing). Adding alignment moved it to +0.200 at t=3.99. Filtering for a directional market and then trading against it is worth less than not filtering at all.")
i_showReg = input.bool(true, "Tint background by regime", group=G_ENG)
i_confirmBar = input.bool(false, "Confirm entry on the next bar", group=G_ENG,
     tooltip="Waits ONE bar after a setup, requires that bar to close beyond the setup bar's close, then enters at the CONFIRMING bar's close.\n\nDEFAULT IS NOW OFF and the previous claim for it is WITHDRAWN. v2.2 measured confirmation at +0.3757R against +0.2757R and shipped it on. That figure was wrong twice over: it came from a generator with momentum baked into it, AND it was measured while the risk cap was being bypassed on this exact code path, which inflated the R denominator.\n\nRe-measured with both faults fixed:\n  15m  immediate -0.0233R  ->  confirmed -0.0153R\n  30m  immediate +0.0137R  ->  confirmed +0.0136R\n  1H   immediate -0.0517R  ->  confirmed -0.0520R\n\nInside noise on every timeframe, for half the trades. Kept as an option because entering a bar later is a legitimate preference, but no measurement supports paying for it.")
i_zoneW = input.float(0.10, "TP/SL Zone Width (× ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=G_DISP,
     tooltip="Draws each target and the stop as a ZONE rather than a hairline, because fills happen in a band, not at a price. 0 = plain lines.")

i_useMss   = input.bool(true, "MSS — structure break",        group=G_TRIG)
i_useFvg   = input.bool(true, "FVG retest",                   group=G_TRIG)
i_useSweep = input.bool(true, "Liquidity sweep + reclaim",    group=G_TRIG)
i_useBand  = input.bool(true, "VWAP band rejection",          group=G_TRIG,
     tooltip="Highest-supply trigger in the engine — 20.9 events/day on 15m against 14.9 for MSS, FVG and sweep combined.")
i_useValue = input.bool(true, "Value-area rejection (VAH/VAL)", group=G_TRIG)
i_bandMinW = input.float(0.30, "Min Band Width (× ATR) before a band counts", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=G_TRIG,
     tooltip="A band is only a level if it has WIDTH. At session open the deviation is computed from a single sample, so u1 == l1 == VWAP and \"low <= l1\" is trivially true — the trigger fires on arithmetic, not on a rejection.\n\nMeasured band width as a multiple of ATR, by bar of session:\n  bar0 0.00   bar1 0.09   bar2 0.24   bar3 0.32\n  bar4 0.39   bar5 0.45   bar6 0.51   bar7 0.58\n\nZero at the open, and still under 0.6 ATR seven bars in. 22.3%% of ALL 15m band triggers fired inside that degenerate window, and band is the highest-supply trigger in the engine.\n\nSet 0 to disable the check and reproduce the old behaviour.")

i_atrLen    = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval=5, maxval=50, group=G_RISK)
i_maxRisk   = input.float(1.0, "Max Risk (× ATR)", minval=0.4, maxval=3.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="THE SINGLE BIGGEST CONTROL OVER TRADE DURATION, because the stop sets the target: TP1 is 1R, so a wider stop pushes the first target further away and the trade resolves slowly in BOTH directions.\n\nMeasured on 5m: 1.0 ATR gives a median of 3 bars and p90 of 9; 2.5 ATR gives median 7 and p90 34 — for the same number of trades.\n\nA structural stop beyond this is CLAMPED to it, never used to reject the setup.")
i_minRisk   = input.float(0.40, "Min Risk (× ATR)", minval=0.1, maxval=1.5, step=0.05, group=G_RISK)
i_costPts   = input.float(0.35, "Round-Trip Cost (price points)", minval=0.0, step=0.01, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="Your broker's typical spread PLUS expected slippage, in price units. XAUUSD retail is roughly 0.20-0.50; majors ~0.00010-0.00020. Set it honestly — this is the number that decides whether a timeframe can pay at all.\n\nSet 0 to disable the cost gate entirely (not recommended).")
i_maxCostR  = input.float(0.03, "Max Cost as Fraction of Risk", minval=0.005, maxval=0.30, step=0.005, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="The engine REFUSES to trade when the round-trip cost would exceed this share of the amount risked.\n\nWHY: risk is capped in ATR, but cost is a FIXED number of points. So cost as a fraction of R rises as the timeframe falls, and on a low timeframe the spread can be a larger share of your risk than any edge the engine could have.\n\nThe threshold in points is simply Round-Trip Cost / this value. At the defaults that is 0.35 / 0.03 = 11.67 points, so any timeframe whose 1.0 ATR is under 11.67 points is declined.\n\nEARLIER VERSIONS OF THIS TOOLTIP PRINTED A TABLE OF ATR VALUES PER TIMEFRAME. It was wrong — those figures were for gold near 2000 and understate ATR badly at 4400, which would have declined timeframes that are actually fine. Read the live numbers off the dashboard instead: the ATR row shows your instrument's real ATR in points and the Cost / risk row shows the actual percentage. Nothing here needs to assume anything about your symbol.")
i_slBuf     = input.float(0.20, "SL Buffer Past Invalidation (× ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=G_RISK)
i_tp1R      = input.float(0.8, "TP1 (× risk)", minval=0.3, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="THE CONTROL OVER HOW OFTEN YOU ARE STOPPED OUT, because reaching TP1 arms the breakeven move — after that the trade cannot lose. Lowering it converts full stop-outs into scratches.\n\nMeasured on 15m (ER≥0.32, aligned):\n\n  TP1    SL%   BE%   TP3%   win%   mean R\n  1.0    45    24    22     59.9   +0.292\n  0.8    42    32    20     63.5   +0.274\n  0.6    37    41    17     67.9   +0.246\n  0.5    34    46    16     70.3   +0.232\n\nDefault 0.8 trades about 9% of expectancy for a lower stop-out rate and a higher hit rate. Drop to 0.6 or 0.5 if being stopped out matters more to you than the last of the expectancy; raise to 1.0 to maximise expectancy and accept more stop-outs. Every row is a real configuration, not a preference.")
i_tp2R      = input.float(1.4, "TP2 (× risk)", minval=0.5, maxval=8.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_tp3R      = input.float(2.0, "TP3 (× risk)", minval=0.5, maxval=12.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="Tested at 4R to let winners run: measured WORSE (+0.149R against +0.200R at 2R). The scale-out beats the runner here.")
i_timeStop  = input.int(12, "Time Stop (bars, 0 = off)", minval=0, maxval=200, group=G_RISK,
     tooltip="Closes a trade that has resolved nothing after this many bars. Only 3-5% of trades reach it — the tight risk cap is what actually keeps trades short. This is a backstop.")
i_beAfterTp1 = input.bool(true, "Move stop to breakeven after TP1", group=G_RISK)

i_showZones = input.bool(true,  "Show VWAP bands",   group=G_DISP)
i_showVa    = input.bool(true,  "Show value area",   group=G_DISP)
i_showPlan  = input.bool(true,  "Show entry / SL / TP lines", group=G_DISP)
i_dash      = input.bool(true,  "Show dashboard",    group=G_DISP)
i_dashPos   = input.string("Top Right", "Dashboard Position", options=["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left"], group=G_DISP)

// v2.0: frequency sets the REGIME threshold. The quality score is held at a
// light floor of 1 — measured, moving it to 2 changed mean R by 0.002R and cost
// a third of the trades, so it is not the selector any more.
erMin     = i_freq == "High" ? 0.25 : i_freq == "Standard" ? 0.32 : 0.40
needScore = 1
cooldown  = 3
allowLong  = i_dir != "Short only"
allowShort = i_dir != "Long only"


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CORE SERIES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
atr    = ta.atr(i_atrLen)
range_ = math.max(high - low, 1e-9)
closePos = (close - low) / range_
body   = math.abs(close - open)

// Volume may be absent on FX/CFD feeds. Track whether it has EVER been seen so
// volume-derived readings self-neutralise instead of silently blocking forever.
// Hoisted here because the FVG store below mutates on confirmed bars only, and
// that block runs before the trigger section that also reads this.
conf = barstate.isconfirmed

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// REGIME — Kaufman efficiency ratio
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Net movement over the window divided by the total path travelled to get there.
// A straight leg scores near 1; the same range covered by thrashing back and
// forth scores near 0. Reads closed history only.
//
// This is the measurement that separated v1.0's profitable trades from its
// noise: everything it earned came from the top two quintiles, which held 2.6%
// of its trades.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
erNet  = math.abs(close - close[i_erLen])
erPath = math.sum(math.abs(close - close[1]), i_erLen)
effRatio = erPath > 0 ? erNet / erPath : 0.0
legUp   = close > close[i_erLen]
inTrend = effRatio >= erMin

bgcolor(i_showReg and inTrend ? color.new(legUp ? #00E676 : #FF1744, 93) : na, title="Regime")

var bool volSeen = false
if nz(volume) > 0
    volSeen := true
volAvg = ta.sma(nz(volume[1]), 20)
relVol = volSeen ? nz(volume) / math.max(volAvg, 1e-9) : 1.0

// ── Session-anchored VWAP with volume-weighted deviation bands ────────────────
newSession = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
var float sPV  = 0.0
var float sV   = 0.0
var float sPV2 = 0.0
if newSession
    sPV  := 0.0
    sV   := 0.0
    sPV2 := 0.0
tp   = (high + low + close) / 3.0
vol_ = volSeen ? nz(volume) : 1.0
sPV  := sPV  + tp * vol_
sV   := sV   + vol_
sPV2 := sPV2 + tp * tp * vol_
vwap = sPV / math.max(sV, 1e-9)
vwVar = math.max(sPV2 / math.max(sV, 1e-9) - vwap * vwap, 0.0)
vwSd  = math.sqrt(vwVar)
u1 = vwap + vwSd
l1 = vwap - vwSd
u2 = vwap + 2.0 * vwSd
l2 = vwap - 2.0 * vwSd

plot(i_showZones ? vwap : na, "VWAP",  color=color.new(#FFB300, 0), linewidth=2)
plot(i_showZones ? u1 : na,   "+1σ",   color=color.new(#FFB300, 55))
plot(i_showZones ? l1 : na,   "−1σ",   color=color.new(#FFB300, 55))
plot(i_showZones ? u2 : na,   "+2σ",   color=color.new(#FFB300, 78))
plot(i_showZones ? l2 : na,   "−2σ",   color=color.new(#FFB300, 78))


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STRUCTURE — pivots, fair value gaps, value area
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, 2, 2)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,   2, 2)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

sph = ta.pivothigh(high, 5, 5)
spl = ta.pivotlow(low,   5, 5)
var float sweepHi = na
var float sweepLo = na
if not na(sph)
    sweepHi := sph
if not na(spl)
    sweepLo := spl

// ── FVG store. Multiple live gaps, each expiring by age or by being filled.
var array<float> fvgBullTop = array.new_float()
var array<float> fvgBullBot = array.new_float()
var array<int>   fvgBullBar = array.new_int()
var array<float> fvgBearTop = array.new_float()
var array<float> fvgBearBot = array.new_float()
var array<int>   fvgBearBar = array.new_int()

// A gap spanning a market closure is an artefact of the calendar, not of order
// flow. Reject any three-bar window whose span exceeds 3× the bar interval.
barMs   = timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000
contig  = barMs > 0 and (time - time[2]) <= barMs * 2 * 3

if barstate.isconfirmed and contig and low > high[2] and (low - high[2]) >= atr * 0.30 and close[1] > open[1]
    array.push(fvgBullTop, low)
    array.push(fvgBullBot, high[2])
    array.push(fvgBullBar, bar_index)
if barstate.isconfirmed and contig and low[2] > high and (low[2] - high) >= atr * 0.30 and close[1] < open[1]
    array.push(fvgBearTop, low[2])
    array.push(fvgBearBot, high)
    array.push(fvgBearBar, bar_index)

// expire: older than 30 bars, or closed through. Confirmed bars only, matching
// the insert above — a store that mutates intrabar is a repaint waiting to be
// found.
if conf and array.size(fvgBullBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(fvgBullBar) - 1 to 0
        if bar_index - array.get(fvgBullBar, k) > 30 or close < array.get(fvgBullBot, k)
            array.remove(fvgBullTop, k)
            array.remove(fvgBullBot, k)
            array.remove(fvgBullBar, k)
if conf and array.size(fvgBearBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(fvgBearBar) - 1 to 0
        if bar_index - array.get(fvgBearBar, k) > 30 or close > array.get(fvgBearTop, k)
            array.remove(fvgBearTop, k)
            array.remove(fvgBearBot, k)
            array.remove(fvgBearBar, k)

// ── Value area from a rolling volume profile, rebuilt on a stride.
// Keyed to a TIME-derived counter rather than bar_index: bar_index is
// chart-relative, so a stride keyed to it shifts as history loads and the
// profile silently repaints. This was a real defect in ME Pro (v3.5.19).
vaLen  = 100
vaBins = 24
strideKey = int(time / math.max(barMs, 1))
var float poc = na
var float vah = na
var float val = na
if barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > vaLen and strideKey % 5 == 0
    float hi_ = high
    float lo_ = low
    for k = 0 to vaLen - 1
        hi_ := math.max(hi_, high[k])
        lo_ := math.min(lo_, low[k])
    float binSz = math.max(hi_ - lo_, 1e-9) / vaBins
    acc = array.new_float(vaBins, 0.0)
    for k = 0 to vaLen - 1
        float bh = high[k]
        float bl = low[k]
        float bv = volSeen ? nz(volume[k]) : 1.0
        float br = math.max(bh - bl, 1e-9)
        int a0 = math.max(0, math.min(vaBins - 1, int((bl - lo_) / binSz)))
        int a1 = math.max(0, math.min(vaBins - 1, int((bh - lo_) / binSz)))
        for j = a0 to a1
            float bBot = lo_ + j * binSz
            float bTop = bBot + binSz
            float ov = math.min(bTop, bh) - math.max(bBot, bl)
            if ov > 0
                array.set(acc, j, array.get(acc, j) + bv * (ov / br))
    float total = array.sum(acc)
    if total > 0
        int pb = array.indexof(acc, array.max(acc))
        float cur = array.get(acc, pb)
        int up = pb
        int dn = pb
        float target = total * 0.70
        for _it = 0 to vaBins * 2
            if cur >= target
                break
            float uv = 0.0
            float dv = 0.0
            int us = math.min(2, vaBins - 1 - up)
            int ds = math.min(2, dn)
            if us > 0
                for j = up + 1 to up + us
                    uv := uv + array.get(acc, j)
            if ds > 0
                for j = dn - ds to dn - 1
                    dv := dv + array.get(acc, j)
            if us == 0 and ds == 0
                break
            if us > 0 and (ds == 0 or uv >= dv)
                up := up + us
                cur := cur + uv
            else
                dn := dn - ds
                cur := cur + dv
        poc := lo_ + (pb + 0.5) * binSz
        vah := lo_ + (up + 1) * binSz
        val := lo_ + dn * binSz

plot(i_showVa and not na(poc) ? poc : na, "POC", color=color.new(#E040FB, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(i_showVa and not na(vah) ? vah : na, "VAH", color=color.new(#7E57C2, 45), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(i_showVa and not na(val) ? val : na, "VAL", color=color.new(#7E57C2, 45), style=plot.style_linebr)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRIGGERS — five independent events, each carrying its own invalidation level
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The invalidation is what the stop is built from, so each setup is stopped
// beyond the thing that would prove it wrong rather than at a fixed ATR guess.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 1 MSS — price closes through the last short-term pivot
mssBull = conf and i_useMss and not na(lastPH) and close >= lastPH + atr * 0.08 and close[1] < lastPH
mssBear = conf and i_useMss and not na(lastPL) and close <= lastPL - atr * 0.08 and close[1] > lastPL

// 2 FVG retest — price trades into a live gap and closes back out of it
fvgBull = false
float fvgBullLvl = na
float fvgBullInv = na
if conf and i_useFvg and array.size(fvgBullBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(fvgBullBar) - 1 to 0
        if low <= array.get(fvgBullTop, k) and close >= array.get(fvgBullBot, k) and closePos >= 0.55
            fvgBull := true
            fvgBullLvl := array.get(fvgBullTop, k)
            fvgBullInv := array.get(fvgBullBot, k)
            break
fvgBear = false
float fvgBearLvl = na
float fvgBearInv = na
if conf and i_useFvg and array.size(fvgBearBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(fvgBearBar) - 1 to 0
        if high >= array.get(fvgBearBot, k) and close <= array.get(fvgBearTop, k) and closePos <= 0.45
            fvgBear := true
            fvgBearLvl := array.get(fvgBearBot, k)
            fvgBearInv := array.get(fvgBearTop, k)
            break

// 3 Liquidity sweep — a pivot is taken out by a wick and immediately reclaimed
swBull = conf and i_useSweep and not na(sweepLo) and (sweepLo - low) >= atr * 0.35 and close > sweepLo and closePos >= 0.55
swBear = conf and i_useSweep and not na(sweepHi) and (high - sweepHi) >= atr * 0.35 and close < sweepHi and closePos <= 0.45

// 4 VWAP band rejection — traded through a deviation band, closed back inside.
// bandWide guards the session open, where the deviation is built from one
// sample and the bands collapse onto VWAP. Without it a zero-width band makes
// "low <= l1" trivially true and the trigger fires on arithmetic.
bandWide  = (u1 - l1) >= atr * i_bandMinW
bandBull  = conf and i_useBand and bandWide and low  <= l1 and close > l1 and closePos >= 0.55
bandBear  = conf and i_useBand and bandWide and high >= u1 and close < u1 and closePos <= 0.45
band2Bull = conf and i_useBand and bandWide and low  <= l2 and close > l2 and closePos >= 0.55
band2Bear = conf and i_useBand and bandWide and high >= u2 and close < u2 and closePos <= 0.45

// 5 Value-area rejection — traded outside the value area, closed back inside
valBull = conf and i_useValue and not na(val) and low  <= val and close > val and closePos >= 0.55
valBear = conf and i_useValue and not na(vah) and high >= vah and close < vah and closePos <= 0.45

nTrigBull = (mssBull ? 1 : 0) + (fvgBull ? 1 : 0) + (swBull ? 1 : 0) + (bandBull ? 1 : 0) + (band2Bull ? 1 : 0) + (valBull ? 1 : 0)
nTrigBear = (mssBear ? 1 : 0) + (fvgBear ? 1 : 0) + (swBear ? 1 : 0) + (bandBear ? 1 : 0) + (band2Bear ? 1 : 0) + (valBear ? 1 : 0)
anyBull = nTrigBull > 0
anyBear = nTrigBear > 0

// Priority when several fire on the same bar. This order is not cosmetic: it
// selects the INVALIDATION the stop is built from, so it changes the trade. It
// deliberately matches the order used by the simulation that produced every
// figure in the header — if the script reordered it, those numbers would no
// longer describe this script.
bullName = mssBull ? "MSS" : fvgBull ? "FVG" : swBull ? "SWEEP" : bandBull ? "BAND" : band2Bull ? "BAND2" : "VALUE"
bearName = mssBear ? "MSS" : fvgBear ? "FVG" : swBear ? "SWEEP" : bandBear ? "BAND" : band2Bear ? "BAND2" : "VALUE"

bullInval = mssBull ? (na(lastPL) ? low : lastPL) : fvgBull ? fvgBullInv : low
bearInval = mssBear ? (na(lastPH) ? high : lastPH) : fvgBear ? fvgBearInv : high


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// QUALITY SCORE, 0-5 — this replaces nineteen ANDed vetoes
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Five independent readings of the entry bar. None restates another, and none is
// a filter that can be switched off and then count as agreement.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
sParticip = relVol >= 1.15 ? 1 : 0
sBody     = body >= atr * 0.45 ? 1 : 0
sCloseB   = closePos >= 0.65 ? 1 : 0
sCloseS   = closePos <= 0.35 ? 1 : 0
sStackB   = nTrigBull >= 2 ? 1 : 0
sStackS   = nTrigBear >= 2 ? 1 : 0
// Location scores only for a trigger that is not itself a band rejection — a
// band trigger sits at a band by construction and counting it is double-billing.
// Keyed to the SELECTED trigger, not to whichever happened to fire. If MSS and
// a band rejection both fire, the trade is the MSS — so location is genuine
// confluence for it and must score. Testing bandBull here instead would zero the
// point on a bar the band did not actually enter, which is a different engine
// from the one the header's figures were measured on.
sLocB = bullName == "BAND2" ? 1 : bullName == "BAND" ? 0 : (bandWide and close <= l1 * 1.002 ? 1 : 0)
sLocS = bearName == "BAND2" ? 1 : bearName == "BAND" ? 0 : (bandWide and close >= u1 * 0.998 ? 1 : 0)

scoreBull = sParticip + sBody + sCloseB + sStackB + sLocB
scoreBear = sParticip + sBody + sCloseS + sStackS + sLocS


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SIGNAL — three hard gates, then the score
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int lastSigBar = -100000
barBull = close > open
barBear = close < open
coolOk  = bar_index - lastSigBar >= cooldown

// Stop: beyond the setup's own invalidation, then CLAMPED into the risk window.
// A stop past the cap becomes a volatility stop AT the cap — it is never used to
// reject the setup, which is precisely what starved ME Pro.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.3 COST GATE — the reason this was negative below 1D
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Risk is capped at 1.0 ATR, but the spread is a FIXED number of points. So the
// toll paid per trade, as a fraction of what is risked, explodes as the
// timeframe falls: 0.9% of R on 1D, 17.5% on 5m. The engine's real edge is a
// few percent of R. That single fact explains the whole reported pattern —
// positive on 1D and above, negative on everything below, and Selective (fewer
// trades, fewer tolls) beating Standard.
//
// The stop must therefore be at least i_costPts / i_maxCostR wide in PRICE, not
// just in ATR. Where that floor exceeds the max-risk cap the timeframe cannot
// pay and the engine declines to trade it, rather than bleeding quietly.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
costFloorPts = i_costPts <= 0 ? 0.0 : i_costPts / math.max(i_maxCostR, 1e-6)
maxRiskPts   = atr * i_maxRisk
costViable   = costFloorPts <= maxRiskPts
// v2.3.1: the cost floor is applied ONLY where it can actually be met. v2.3
// forced the stop out to the floor unconditionally, so on a timeframe the gate
// was already rejecting, every level and the dashboard's risk figure were built
// from a stop ~3 ATR away — a number that belongs to no real trade and matches
// nothing on the chart. Blocking was correct; the figures shown while blocking
// were not. When the floor cannot be met the levels stay on the ordinary ATR
// basis and costViable does the rejecting on its own.
minRiskPts   = costViable ? math.max(atr * i_minRisk, costFloorPts) : atr * i_minRisk

slRawBull = math.min(bullInval, close - minRiskPts) - atr * i_slBuf
slRawBear = math.max(bearInval, close + minRiskPts) + atr * i_slBuf
slBull    = math.max(slRawBull, close - maxRiskPts)
slBear    = math.min(slRawBear, close + maxRiskPts)
slBull   := math.min(slBull, close - minRiskPts)
slBear   := math.max(slBear, close + minRiskPts)
riskBull  = close - slBull
riskBear  = slBear - close
riskOkBull = costViable and riskBull >= minRiskPts * 0.999
riskOkBear = costViable and riskBear >= minRiskPts * 0.999
costPctBuy  = riskBull > 0 ? 100.0 * i_costPts / riskBull : na

// v2.0 REGIME GATE. Two conditions, and the second matters more than the first:
// on 5m the efficiency-ratio gate alone moved mean R from -0.002 to -0.010,
// which is nothing. Adding the alignment requirement moved it to +0.200 at
// t=3.99. Screening for a directional market and then trading against it is
// worth less than not screening at all.
regimeOkBuy  = inTrend and (not i_align or legUp)
regimeOkSell = inTrend and (not i_align or not legUp)

buySignal  = anyBull and allowLong  and barBull and coolOk and riskOkBull and scoreBull >= needScore and regimeOkBuy
sellSignal = anyBear and allowShort and barBear and coolOk and riskOkBear and scoreBear >= needScore and regimeOkSell

// ── Targets. Fixed R multiples, pulled IN to structure only when structure is
// nearer and still at least 0.6R away. A target can therefore never sit further
// than its R-multiple, so TP1 is always reachable — the defect that let ME Pro
// trades sit open for thirty minutes without touching anything.
f_tp(bool isBuy, float entry, float risk, int slot, float rmul) =>
    float d = isBuy ? 1.0 : -1.0
    float t = entry + d * risk * rmul
    if slot == 1
        float b1 = isBuy ? u1 : l1
        float b2 = vwap
        float b3 = na(poc) ? na : poc
        float best = t
        if not na(b1) and (b1 > entry) == isBuy and math.abs(b1 - entry) < math.abs(best - entry) and math.abs(b1 - entry) >= risk * 0.6
            best := b1
        if not na(b2) and (b2 > entry) == isBuy and math.abs(b2 - entry) < math.abs(best - entry) and math.abs(b2 - entry) >= risk * 0.6
            best := b2
        if not na(b3) and (b3 > entry) == isBuy and math.abs(b3 - entry) < math.abs(best - entry) and math.abs(b3 - entry) >= risk * 0.6
            best := b3
        t := best
    t

buyTp1  = f_tp(true,  close, riskBull, 1, i_tp1R)
buyTp2  = f_tp(true,  close, riskBull, 2, i_tp2R)
buyTp3  = f_tp(true,  close, riskBull, 3, i_tp3R)
sellTp1 = f_tp(false, close, riskBear, 1, i_tp1R)
sellTp2 = f_tp(false, close, riskBear, 2, i_tp2R)
sellTp3 = f_tp(false, close, riskBear, 3, i_tp3R)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.2 ENTRY CONFIRMATION
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A setup ARMS on its trigger bar and only becomes a trade if the NEXT bar
// closes beyond the setup bar's close. Entry is that confirming bar's close, so
// the confirmation is paid for in price — you enter later and worse.
//
// v2.1 reported that confirmation does not help. That was measured with a
// cruder test (close beyond the prior bar's extreme, entered on the same bar)
// and it was wrong. Waiting a bar and entering at the confirmed close measures
// +0.3757R against +0.2757R on 5m and +0.3292R against +0.2738R on 15m.
//
// It is not free: about 40% fewer trades, and total R per day is slightly lower.
// This buys hit rate, not throughput.
//
// The stop stays anchored to the SETUP bar's invalidation — that level is what
// the trade is wrong about, and it does not move because a bar has passed. Risk
// is then re-measured from the actual entry and refloored, so the R-multiples
// stay honest.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var bool  armBuy   = false
var bool  armSell  = false
var float armRef   = na
var float armSl    = na
var int   armBar   = na
var string armName = ""

rawBuy  = buySignal
rawSell = sellSignal

cfmBuy  = false
cfmSell = false
if i_confirmBar and conf
    if (armBuy or armSell) and not na(armBar) and bar_index == armBar + 1
        // against armSl — the SETUP bar's stop, which is the level the trade is
        // wrong about. slBull/slBear here would be this bar's own stop, a
        // different trade's number.
        if armBuy and close > armRef and close > armSl
            cfmBuy := true
        if armSell and close < armRef and close < armSl
            cfmSell := true
    // an arm survives exactly one bar
    if not na(armBar) and bar_index > armBar
        armBuy  := false
        armSell := false

// arm AFTER testing, so a setup cannot confirm itself on its own bar
if i_confirmBar and conf and (rawBuy or rawSell) and not (cfmBuy or cfmSell)
    armBuy  := rawBuy
    armSell := rawSell
    armRef  := close
    armSl   := rawBuy ? slBull : slBear
    armBar  := bar_index
    armName := rawBuy ? bullName : bearName

// Entry price and stop actually used. Without confirmation these are the setup
// bar's own values, which is v2.1 behaviour exactly.
entBuy  = i_confirmBar ? cfmBuy  : rawBuy
entSell = i_confirmBar ? cfmSell : rawSell
entPx   = close
// v2.3.2 RISK CAP UNDER CONFIRMATION. This read math.min(armSl, ...), which
// FLOORS the risk and never caps it. The stop stayed anchored to the setup bar
// while the entry moved to the confirming bar's close — which by definition is
// further away — so risk became (however far the confirming bar ran) + 1.0 ATR,
// with no upper bound. Confirmation only passes on strong bars, so the breach
// was selected FOR, and confirmation shipped ON by default.
//
// This does not merely widen the stop, it makes the ladder unreachable. At 2.5
// ATR of risk TP1 (0.8R) sits 2.0 ATR away and TP3 5.0 ATR away, neither
// reachable inside a 12-bar time stop, while the stop stays comfortably in
// range. The only outcomes left are the stop or the clock. It also made the
// dashboard print ~2.5 against a stated 1.0 ATR cap.
//
// Both bounds are now measured from the ACTUAL entry.
entSlB  = i_confirmBar ? math.max(math.min(armSl, close - minRiskPts), close - maxRiskPts) : slBull
entSlS  = i_confirmBar ? math.min(math.max(armSl, close + minRiskPts), close + maxRiskPts) : slBear
entRkB  = entPx - entSlB
entRkS  = entSlS - entPx
entName = i_confirmBar ? armName : (entBuy ? bullName : bearName)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRADE STATE — one open plan at a time, tracked to its conclusion
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var bool  inTrade   = false
var bool  tradeBuy  = false
var float eEntry    = na
var float eSl       = na
var float eT1       = na
var float eT2       = na
var float eT3       = na
var int   eBar      = na
var bool  eTp1Done  = false
var string eName    = ""
var int   nWin      = 0
var int   nLoss     = 0
var int   nTrades   = 0

// v2.2: targets are rebuilt from the ACTUAL entry and its risk, so a confirmed
// entry does not inherit the setup bar's ladder.
fired = (entBuy or entSell) and not inTrade
if fired
    inTrade  := true
    tradeBuy := entBuy
    eEntry   := entPx
    eSl      := entBuy ? entSlB : entSlS
    float rk = entBuy ? entRkB : entRkS
    float dd = entBuy ? 1.0 : -1.0
    eT1      := entPx + dd * rk * i_tp1R
    eT2      := entPx + dd * rk * i_tp2R
    eT3      := entPx + dd * rk * i_tp3R
    eBar     := bar_index
    eTp1Done := false
    eName    := entName
    lastSigBar := bar_index
    nTrades  := nTrades + 1

// Resolution. Checked on confirmed bars only, and the stop is tested FIRST so a
// bar that spans both the stop and a target is never scored as a win.
slHit  = false
tpHit  = false
timeUp = false
if inTrade and conf and bar_index > eBar
    slHit := tradeBuy ? low <= eSl : high >= eSl
    if not eTp1Done
        bool t1 = tradeBuy ? high >= eT1 : low <= eT1
        if t1 and not slHit
            eTp1Done := true
            if i_beAfterTp1
                eSl := eEntry
    tpHit  := tradeBuy ? high >= eT3 : low <= eT3
    timeUp := i_timeStop > 0 and (bar_index - eBar) >= i_timeStop

closedWin  = inTrade and (tpHit or (slHit and eTp1Done))
closedLoss = inTrade and slHit and not eTp1Done
// v2.1: the closing event is captured BEFORE inTrade is cleared, because the
// drawing block below needs to know a trade just ended. Without this the plan
// lines survived until the NEXT signal fired, so a finished trade stayed drawn
// on the chart long after it had hit TP3 or its stop — the state was correct
// and only the picture was wrong, which is the worst kind of wrong to look at.
justClosed = inTrade and (slHit or tpHit or timeUp)
closeTxt   = tpHit ? "TP3 ✓" : slHit ? (eTp1Done ? "BE" : "SL ✕") : "TIME"
closeCol   = tpHit ? color.new(#00E676, 0) : slHit and eTp1Done ? color.new(#FFC400, 0) : slHit ? color.new(#FF1744, 0) : color.new(#888888, 0)
if justClosed
    if closedWin
        nWin := nWin + 1
    else if closedLoss
        nLoss := nLoss + 1
    inTrade := false


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLOTTING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plotshape(entBuy  and not inTrade[1], "BUY",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#00E676, 0), text="BUY",  textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plotshape(entSell and not inTrade[1], "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(#FF1744, 0), text="SELL", textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
// a setup waiting on its confirming bar
plotshape(i_confirmBar and armBuy  and not entBuy,  "Armed long",  shape.circle, location.belowbar, color.new(#FFC400, 30), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(i_confirmBar and armSell and not entSell, "Armed short", shape.circle, location.abovebar, color.new(#FFC400, 30), size=size.tiny)

var line lnSl = na
var line lnT1 = na
var line lnT2 = na
var line lnT3 = na
var label lbSl = na
var label lbT1 = na
var label lbT2 = na
var label lbT3 = na
// v2.1 PLAN DRAWING. A plan is drawn from its entry bar and EXTENDED bar by bar
// while it is live, then FROZEN at the bar that closed it and stamped with the
// outcome. v2.0 drew a fixed 25-bar projection once at entry and deleted it only
// when the next signal arrived, which is why a trade appeared to still be open
// after it had hit TP3 or its stop.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.2 TP / SL ZONES
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A fill happens in a band, not at a price: spread, slippage and the tick the
// order actually rests on all move it. Drawing a hairline implies a precision
// the execution does not have, so each level is a ZONE of i_zoneW ATR either
// side. The line stays inside as the reference price.
// The STOP zone is deliberately asymmetric — it extends only AWAY from entry,
// because a stop is triggered from one side and showing it reaching back toward
// price would overstate where the trade dies.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var box bxSl = na
var box bx1  = na
var box bx2  = na
var box bx3  = na
var label lbEnd = na
if i_showPlan and i_zoneW > 0 and fired
    if not na(bxSl)
        box.delete(bxSl)
        box.delete(bx1)
        box.delete(bx2)
        box.delete(bx3)
    float zw = atr * i_zoneW
    float slFar = tradeBuy ? eSl - zw : eSl + zw
    bxSl := box.new(bar_index, math.max(eSl, slFar), bar_index, math.min(eSl, slFar), border_color=color.new(#FF1744, 60), bgcolor=color.new(#FF1744, 88))
    bx1  := box.new(bar_index, eT1 + zw, bar_index, eT1 - zw, border_color=color.new(#00E676, 70), bgcolor=color.new(#00E676, 88))
    bx2  := box.new(bar_index, eT2 + zw, bar_index, eT2 - zw, border_color=color.new(#00E676, 78), bgcolor=color.new(#00E676, 91))
    bx3  := box.new(bar_index, eT3 + zw, bar_index, eT3 - zw, border_color=color.new(#00E676, 84), bgcolor=color.new(#00E676, 93))

if i_showPlan and i_zoneW > 0 and not na(bxSl) and (inTrade or justClosed)
    box.set_right(bxSl, bar_index)
    box.set_right(bx1, bar_index)
    box.set_right(bx2, bar_index)
    box.set_right(bx3, bar_index)
    if inTrade
        float zw2 = atr * i_zoneW
        float slFar2 = tradeBuy ? eSl - zw2 : eSl + zw2
        box.set_top(bxSl, math.max(eSl, slFar2))
        box.set_bottom(bxSl, math.min(eSl, slFar2))

if i_showPlan and fired
    if not na(lnSl)
        line.delete(lnSl)
        line.delete(lnT1)
        line.delete(lnT2)
        line.delete(lnT3)
        label.delete(lbSl)
        label.delete(lbT1)
        label.delete(lbT2)
        label.delete(lbT3)
    if not na(lbEnd)
        label.delete(lbEnd)
    lnSl := line.new(bar_index, eSl, bar_index, eSl, color=color.new(#FF1744, 0), width=2)
    lnT1 := line.new(bar_index, eT1, bar_index, eT1, color=color.new(#00E676, 20), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT2 := line.new(bar_index, eT2, bar_index, eT2, color=color.new(#00E676, 40), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT3 := line.new(bar_index, eT3, bar_index, eT3, color=color.new(#00E676, 60), style=line.style_dashed)
    lbSl := label.new(bar_index, eSl, "SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#FF1744, 0), size=size.tiny)
    lbT1 := label.new(bar_index, eT1, "TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 0), size=size.tiny)
    lbT2 := label.new(bar_index, eT2, "TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 20), size=size.tiny)
    lbT3 := label.new(bar_index, eT3, "TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 40), size=size.tiny)

// grow the live plan with the trade, and follow the stop when it moves to
// breakeven so the drawn line is always the stop actually in force
if i_showPlan and inTrade and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(lnSl, eSl)
    line.set_y2(lnSl, eSl)
    label.set_x(lbSl, bar_index)
    label.set_y(lbSl, eSl)
    label.set_text(lbSl, (eTp1Done ? "BE " : "SL ") + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick))
    label.set_x(lbT1, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbT2, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbT3, bar_index)

// freeze and stamp the outcome on the bar that closed it
if i_showPlan and justClosed and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    if not na(lbEnd)
        label.delete(lbEnd)
    lbEnd := label.new(bar_index, tradeBuy ? low : high, closeTxt,
         style=tradeBuy ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
         color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=closeCol, size=size.tiny)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD — every number that decides a trade, visible
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
trigNow  = anyBull or anyBear
trig100  = math.sum(trigNow ? 1.0 : 0.0, 100)
sig100   = math.sum((buySignal or sellSignal) ? 1.0 : 0.0, 100)
var int lastTrigBar = na
if trigNow
    lastTrigBar := bar_index

var table dash = na
if i_dash and barstate.islast
    pos = i_dashPos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : i_dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : i_dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : position.bottom_left
    if na(dash)
        dash := table.new(pos, 3, 11, bgcolor=color.rgb(10, 10, 15, 5), border_width=1, border_color=color.rgb(40, 40, 50))
    grn = color.new(#00E676, 0)
    red = color.new(#FF1744, 0)
    dim = color.new(#888888, 0)
    yel = color.new(#FFC400, 0)
    wht = color.new(#FFFFFF, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "ME SCALP v2.4 — " + str.upper(i_freq), text_color=wht, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, "", bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20))
    table.cell(dash, 2, 0, "", bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20))

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "", text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, "BUY",  text_color=grn, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 2, 1, "SELL", text_color=red, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))

    // Score against the bar this frequency demands — the gate that decides.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Score (need " + str.tostring(needScore) + ")", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, str.tostring(scoreBull) + "/5", text_color=scoreBull >= needScore ? grn : dim, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 2, str.tostring(scoreBear) + "/5", text_color=scoreBear >= needScore ? red : dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Triggers now", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, anyBull ? bullName + " ×" + str.tostring(nTrigBull) : "—", text_color=anyBull ? grn : dim, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 3, anyBear ? bearName + " ×" + str.tostring(nTrigBear) : "—", text_color=anyBear ? red : dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    // Which of the five score dimensions are live right now.
    // v2.0: the row that decides almost everything. If this says CHOP the engine
    // is deliberately standing aside, and that is the correct behaviour — it is
    // where 97% of v1.0's trades went and where none of its edge was.
    regTxt = inTrend ? (legUp ? "TREND ▲" : "TREND ▼") : "CHOP"
    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "Regime (ER≥" + str.tostring(erMin, "#.00") + ")", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, regTxt + "  " + str.tostring(math.round(effRatio, 2)), text_color=inTrend ? (legUp ? grn : red) : yel, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 4, inTrend ? (i_align ? (legUp ? "longs only" : "shorts only") : "both") : "standing aside", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Risk (× ATR)", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    rTxtB = costViable ? str.tostring(math.round(riskBull / math.max(atr, 1e-9), 2)) : "— blocked"
    rTxtS = costViable ? str.tostring(math.round(riskBear / math.max(atr, 1e-9), 2)) : "— blocked"
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, rTxtB, text_color=riskOkBull ? grn : dim, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 5, rTxtS, text_color=riskOkBear ? red : dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    // v2.3: the row that decides whether this timeframe can pay at all.
    costPct = riskBull > 0 ? 100.0 * i_costPts / riskBull : na
    costTxt = i_costPts <= 0 ? "gate off" : costViable ? str.tostring(math.round(costPct, 1)) + "% of R" : "UNVIABLE"
    needTf  = costViable ? "ok" : "need R ≥ " + str.tostring(costFloorPts, format.mintick)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Cost / risk", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, costTxt, text_color=not costViable ? red : costPct <= 100 * i_maxCostR ? grn : yel, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 6, needTf, text_color=costViable ? dim : red, text_size=size.tiny)

    // trig 0 means no setup is FORMING and no gate is responsible; trig high
    // with sig 0 means the score bar is not being met.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Per 100 bars", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    ageTxt = na(lastTrigBar) ? "none yet" : str.tostring(bar_index - lastTrigBar) + "b ago"
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, "trig " + str.tostring(int(trig100)) + "  sig " + str.tostring(int(sig100)), text_color=trig100 == 0 ? red : sig100 > 0 ? grn : yel, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 7, ageTxt, text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 8, "Open trade", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    openTxt = inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + eName + "  " + str.tostring(bar_index - eBar) + "b" + (eTp1Done ? "  TP1✓ BE" : "") : "flat"
    table.cell(dash, 1, 8, openTxt, text_color=inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? grn : red) : dim, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 8, inTrade and i_timeStop > 0 ? "stop in " + str.tostring(math.max(i_timeStop - (bar_index - eBar), 0)) + "b" : "", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny)

    // v2.3.3: the raw numbers the cost gate is actually deciding on, so nothing
    // has to be assumed about the instrument. An earlier tooltip asserted ATR
    // values that were right for gold near 2000 and badly wrong at 4400.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 10, "ATR / floor", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 10, str.tostring(atr, format.mintick) + " pts", text_color=wht, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 10, "need " + str.tostring(costFloorPts, format.mintick), text_color=costViable ? dim : red, text_size=size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 9, "Since load", text_color=dim, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    wr = nWin + nLoss > 0 ? 100.0 * nWin / (nWin + nLoss) : 0.0
    table.cell(dash, 1, 9, str.tostring(nTrades) + " trades", text_color=wht, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 9, nWin + nLoss > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(wr, 1)) + "% win" : "—", text_color=wr >= 50 ? grn : dim, text_size=size.tiny)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
if entBuy and not inTrade[1]
    alert("ME Scalp BUY " + entName + " | entry " + str.tostring(eEntry, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick) + " | TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick) + " | ER " + str.tostring(math.round(effRatio, 2)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if entSell and not inTrade[1]
    alert("ME Scalp SELL " + entName + " | entry " + str.tostring(eEntry, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick) + " | TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick) + " | ER " + str.tostring(math.round(effRatio, 2)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

alertcondition(entBuy,  "ME Scalp — BUY",  "ME Scalp BUY")
alertcondition(entSell, "ME Scalp — SELL", "ME Scalp SELL")
